title the loop paths follow the fold, and the round writes itself down twice
prompt Keaton asked what our original intention was and what the synthesized intention is now, written as a Gauge external-research piece and a siloed active-development piece, and asked to update the recursion loop's inner and outer paths for the tools/ag/agent* and tools/l/launch_claude* scripts, molting or debriding any path reference that moved.
think Opened with a cold roster run rather than trusting the staged tree. 30 green, one red -- phantom_path naming linengrow/lib_session_root_nest_cue_jam.rye.
think Read the path before judging it. It is a symlink into glow/.cache/ that tools/s/stoa71_glow_import_seam_witness.rish and tools/t/tube05_apk_pack_witness.rish CREATE while they run, and .gitignore line 196 names it. So running the roster manufactured the artifact the next run reported.
think The scan already carried two hand-written guesses about which rooms are generated -- seed/ and any dot-segment path. Replaced the guessing with a question to git: git check-ignore -q, spent only on the handful of literals that resolve here and stand untracked, which is two.
think Proved the rule both ways rather than only the free side. The control pen builds the exact shape (a lowered .rye in glow/.cache/, a symlink into linengrow/, a .gitignore line naming it, a tool reading it) and checks it passes; then builds the same shape with the ignore rule lifted and checks it is refused. Ten cases now.
think Booked REDS %172 and folded %169 to archive to keep the living pin under its 24,576-byte bound; headline re-measured 171 to 172 by the ledger's own guard rather than by hand.
think Measured the loop paths before repairing them. Both loop entries were already correct after the fold: launch-claude.rish calls bash tools/ag/agent-jail.sh claude, launch-claude-season.rish prints the outer-shell loop naming ./tools/ag/agent-jail.sh and renders through tools/s/stream_render.jq, and agent-jail.sh climbs $(dirname "$0")/../.. which is two levels and right at tools/ag/.
think Ran the repointer dry: 1,934 folded files mapped, 3,330 candidates, zero left to rewrite. So the 197 remaining flat-looking references are ones it correctly declines, and each wanted reading rather than sweeping.
think Sorted those 197 by hand into four kinds -- machine-local copies whose instructions moved (SOURCE.md, enclosure-editors.md, the two .example headers), one module carrying an elder name (ember/README.md still said Kiln and pointed at tools/oven_corpus_lap*.rish), deliberate absence assertions (seva_rename_witness names two elder paths to prove they are gone), and synthetic strings inside control cases (tools/foo.rish, tools/thing_lap3.rish).
think Left Skate alone in ember/README.md. The Skate-to-Surf rename is seated yet its sweep is a separate round, and half-sweeping a name across one file is worse than leaving it whole.
think Wrote the two syntheses at Gauge Field and measured both with the guard's own measure function rather than by feel. External research 26% negative sentences, the round record 5%, against a Field target of 30%.
obs The day reads as one subject end to end. Twenty-three ledger rows, %150 through %172, every one in the measuring equipment or in the tree's description of itself, and none in the code the equipment watches. The original ask was one chmod and one rule.
obs The self-inflicted red is the most portable finding of the lap: an instrument with side effects wants those side effects on its own exemption list, derived from a declaration rather than guessed from a name.
obs The external-research piece is written for a generic Acme Corporation employee per the always-on rule, so it names no person and carries a falsifier -- a second audit within a month finding substantially fewer than twenty-three rows, clustered in whatever class this one failed to name.
